      "hints": [
        "Take logarithms of both sides so the variable exponents become multipliers.",
        "Use $\\ln(4\\cdot7^x)=\\ln4+x\\ln7$ and $\\ln(5^{3-2x})=(3-2x)\\ln5$.",
        "Collect the terms containing $x$ into a linear equation and round only the final value to 3 decimal places."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Take the natural logarithm of both sides of the equation $5^{3-2x} = 4(7^x)$:\n$$\\ln\\left(5^{3-2x}\\right) = \\ln\\left(4 \\cdot 7^x\\right)$$",
        "Apply the logarithm laws $\\ln(a^b) = b\\ln a$ and $\\ln(ab) = \\ln a + \\ln b$:\n$$(3 - 2x)\\ln 5 = \\ln 4 + x\\ln 7$$",
        "Expand the left-hand side:\n$$3\\ln 5 - 2x\\ln 5 = \\ln 4 + x\\ln 7$$",
        "Collect terms containing $x$ on one side and constant terms on the other side:\n$$3\\ln 5 - \\ln 4 = x\\ln 7 + 2x\\ln 5$$\n$$x(\\ln 7 + 2\\ln 5) = 3\\ln 5 - \\ln 4$$",
        "Isolate $x$:\n$$x = \\dfrac{3\\ln 5 - \\ln 4}{\\ln 7 + 2\\ln 5}$$",
        "Calculate the intermediate numerical values:\n- $\\ln 5 \\approx 1.609438 \\implies 3\\ln 5 \\approx 4.828314$\n- $\\ln 4 \\approx 1.386294$\n- $\\text{Numerator} = 4.828314 - 1.386294 = 3.442020$\n- $\\ln 7 \\approx 1.945910 \\implies 2\\ln 5 \\approx 3.218876$\n- $\\text{Denominator} = 1.945910 + 3.218876 = 5.164786$",
        "Evaluate the quotient:\n$$x = \\dfrac{3.442020}{5.164786} \\approx 0.666440$$",
        "Round to 3 decimal places:\n$$x \\approx 0.666$$"
      ],
